&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title&lt;/strong&gt;: Account Executive&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary&lt;/strong&gt;: $140-175k OTE + Equity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;: New York City (In-Person)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Terial:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Terial is disrupting the ~$13+ trillion global construction industry with AI workflow automation software for commercial roofers and contractors. Our platform replaces the fragmented patchwork of spreadsheets, legacy software, and disconnected point solutions that break as companies scale, helping contractors run more efficient and profitable operations. Backed by top-tier investors and serving hundreds of customers nationwide, we’re scaling rapidly and looking to grow our sales team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a high-impact, collaborative full-cycle &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Account Executive&lt;/span&gt; to help accelerate our growth and expand our presence in the commercial roofing industry. You’ll be joining a fast-growing core team at a pivotal moment, building on a proven go-to-market motion while bringing fresh ideas to deepen customer relationships and drive revenue. This role offers significant ownership, close collaboration with leadership, and the opportunity to grow alongside a company that’s scaling rapidly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Customer Acquisition&lt;/span&gt;: Own the end-to-end sales cycle, from prospecting and qualifying leads to negotiating and closing deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Market Leadership&lt;/span&gt;: Develop and execute strategies to establish Terial as the go-to solution for commercial contractors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Customer-Centric Selling&lt;/span&gt;: Build strong relationships with customers by understanding their needs and positioning Terial’s value effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Pipeline Development&lt;/span&gt;: Collaborate with the team to create and refine outbound and inbound lead generation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Feedback Loop&lt;/span&gt;: Act as the voice of the customer, providing critical feedback to influence product development and roadmap decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Team Building&lt;/span&gt;: Lay the groundwork for scaling the sales team, including designing sales processes and mentoring future hires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in B2B SaaS sales at a startup, including at least 1+ year of AE experience, with a proven track record of meeting or exceeding quota.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to SMB or mid-market customers; familiarity with construction and proptech is a strong plus but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An entrepreneurial mindset: comfortable navigating ambiguity and wearing multiple hats in a fast-paced startup environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native mindset, with demonstrated ability to leverage AI tools to increase output, improve workflows, and drive insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to work cross-functionally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-driven approach to sales, with proficiency in CRM tools and a focus on continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel (upwards of 20% of the time) to conferences, seminars and in-person events with prospects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for learning and excitement about building solutions for an industry ready for transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $140,000 - $175,000 OTE, commensurate with experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Generous equity compensation, giving you a stake in our shared success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Benefits&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive medical, vision and dental insurance plans offered (with up to 100% covered)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weekly team lunch at NYC office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Terial, you&#39;ll help redefine the future of the built world while working at the intersection of climate, real estate, and fintech. Beyond the chance to build and scale a transformative product, you’ll join a passionate, driven team that values collaboration, innovation, and meaningful impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re a driven sales professional ready to make your mark as an Account Executive, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title&lt;/strong&gt;: Senior Customer Success Manager (CSM)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary&lt;/strong&gt;: $120-150k base annually + equity &amp;amp; commissions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;: New York City (In-Person)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Terial:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Terial is disrupting the ~$13+ trillion global construction industry with AI-powered workflow automation software for commercial roofers and contractors. Our platform replaces the fragmented patchwork of spreadsheets, legacy software, and disconnected point solutions that break as companies scale, helping contractors run more efficient and profitable operations. Backed by top-tier investors and serving hundreds of customers nationwide, we’re scaling rapidly and looking to grow our customer success team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Senior Customer Success Manager (CSM)&lt;/span&gt;, you will own the complete post-sale lifecycle for a portfolio of Mid-Market and Enterprise commercial roofing clients, from onboarding and implementation through customer support, ongoing account management, Quarterly Business Reviews, and renewals. You will lead complex, multi-stakeholder implementations delivered virtually or in person, and serve as a trusted advisor to executive and operational stakeholders. You will also carry direct accountability for retention and expansion revenue across your book of business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual-contributor role for someone who wants full ownership of the customer journey for our most strategic accounts. You will report to our Head of Customer Success and work closely with our CEO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Onboarding &amp;amp; Implementation&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Own end-to-end onboarding and implementation for Mid-Market and Enterprise accounts, delivered virtually or in person, guiding multi-stakeholder teams from kickoff through go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Training &amp;amp; Enablement&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Design and deliver structured virtual and on-site training programs, build customer-facing resources, and enable users at every level - from executives and admins to field foremen. Up to ~25% travel expected.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Relationship Management&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact and trusted advisor for senior executives and operational leaders, building long-term trust and advocacy across the account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Ongoing Account Ownership&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Own the complete customer lifecycle post-onboarding, including customer support, regular cadence syncs, account health monitoring, and proactive risk mitigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Quarterly Business Reviews&lt;/span&gt;: Lead QBRs and strategic account reviews, presenting ROI and value narratives that keep executive stakeholders engaged and bought in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Renewals &amp;amp; Expansion&lt;/span&gt;: Own the full renewal process and carry a quota for retention and expansion revenue across your portfolio, identifying and closing upsell and cross-sell opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Support &amp;amp; Issue Resolution&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Manage escalations, triage product issues with Engineering, and keep customers informed until resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Feedback &amp;amp; Collaboration&lt;/span&gt;: Surface customer insights to Product and Engineering to help shape Terial’s roadmap and improve the user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Process &amp;amp; Playbook Leadership&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Take a lead role in building and refining Customer Success playbooks and best practices as we scale, and serve as a senior voice on the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-8+ years of combined experience across Customer Success, Account Management, and Implementation in a B2B SaaS environment, with direct experience onboarding and managing Mid-Market and Enterprise accounts; early-stage startup experience preferred. Working with software for the Trades experience is a plus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in Customer Success at an early stage startup &amp;amp; 2+ years of experience at a scaled startup or in a non-startup environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience managing a mid-market and/or enterprise-level B2B SaaS book of business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record carrying and hitting renewal and expansion revenue targets, ideally in a quota-carrying Customer Success or Account Management role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success onboarding and implementing complex, multi-stakeholder accounts, with strong project management skills across multiple concurrent implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in Customer Success for either a multi-moduled SaaS product or multiple products within the same book of business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, consultative approach to client relationships and problem-solving, with a metrics-driven mindset that translates customer outcomes into measurable business results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating as an individual contributor - someone who can own ambiguity, set the example for the team, and contribute to CS process and playbooks as the team scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, including experience presenting to and influencing C-suite and senior operational stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel for key customer onboarding, training, and QBR engagements, roughly 25%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $120,000 - $150,000 per annum, commensurate with experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Generous equity compensation, giving you a stake in our shared success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Benefits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive medical, vision and dental insurance plans offered (with up to 100% covered)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work environment (Monday through Thursday in-person; Fridays remote - 8:30am-6pm expectation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weekly team lunch at NYC office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Terial, you’ll help redefine the future of the built world leveraging AI while working at the intersection of climate, real estate, and fintech. As a senior member of our Customer Success team, you’ll have outsized influence over how we onboard and grow our most strategic accounts - and you’ll do it alongside a passionate, driven team that values collaboration, innovation, and meaningful impact. If you’re excited to blend onboarding expertise, strategic account ownership, and revenue accountability to drive lasting customer outcomes, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
